From 3b5c43ecbda63afc368fae9674021a282cf58838 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The Combat room: 36 tiles under one piece

The other room that contained nothing. 25,000 coins and 32 Construction bought a painted square on
the floor and sixteen clicks that said "Nothing interesting happens".

Boxing ring, Fencing ring, Combat ring and the Balance beam, at OSRS's levels, materials and
experience, plus the Glove rack on the storage hotspot. Ranging pedestals are NOT here: the template
keeps four tiles for them and this cache has no art for any of it.

THE BOLT OF CLOTH did not exist and three of the four rings are made of it. New obj, sold by the
Sawmill operator for 650 - which is both where OSRS sells it and where the planks already come from,
so it went into his dialogue beside the saw and the hammer. 377's existing "Cloth" whose description
is literally "A bolt of cloth" is the Regicide quest item, gated behind the quest and eaten by it.

A RING IS ONE PIECE STANDING ON 36 TILES, which the furniture system could not express: ~poh_furn_show
has one loc_add per item. Two things made it fit. The placement is a proc, through the same "show"
hand-off the portal frames use. And the piece is ANCHORED: sixteen hotspots and one ring, so a new
"anchor" key stores it at the room's own (0,0) - a tile nothing is ever built on, because the ring
starts at (1,1) - rather than at whichever tile was clicked. ~poh_furn_click is now a door into
~poh_furn_click_at. Removal is the ring's own for the same reason, and a family can now name its
removal proc.

THE ROTATION IS DONE AT RUNTIME because a room can be built at any of four rotations. The table is in
template space and the arithmetic is transcribed from the engine rather than worked out again -
GameMap.rotateZoneX/rotateZoneZ and the newAngle line beside them. Group 59 checks all four cases
literally: a ring that lays itself sideways in a turned room is invisible until someone builds a room
the other way round.

WHAT SAID WHICH TILE IS WHICH. Nineteen hotspot locs, all named "Combat ring space", and nothing in
the config distinguishing them. Their MODEL SIZES do, matched against the pieces in poh.loc: 1785 is
the ring wall, 577 a corner mat, 335 a side mat, 45 a middle mat. The geometry says the same thing and
the generator refuses to write if the two readings disagree.

AND THREE OF THE NINETEEN ARE EMPTY - zero-length .ob2 files that render nothing and cannot be
clicked. They were never dead hotspots: they are placement targets. loc474_15285's three tiles are
where the balance beam goes, loc474_15283/15284's four are the ranging pedestals. So the room had
sixteen dead clicks, not nineteen, and the audit figure of 93 is really 89. The repo-wide count is
now 68.

ONE INFERENCE, labelled as one: boxing's white and corner locs are byte-identical and red and blue
are rope recolours, and which tile wears which is recorded nowhere. Red corner, blue corner opposite,
two neutral, white rope between - what a boxing ring looks like. One table in gencombatring.py.

Climbing in and out is real and had to be, or the ring is a box you cannot get into. Everything else
OSRS does in a ring needs a second player, so the beam and the ring say so - the answer the games
room and the throne room lever already give.

rs2check 0 ERROR / 0 CHECK over 1,670 scripts and 459 configs; poh_battery ALL PASS (59 groups);
poh_mutate every mutation caught, eleven of them new.

